    "title": "Tyler's new road markings designed to cut accidents, boost flow - NewsBreak",
    "text": "TYLER, Texas ( KETK ) — The City of Tyler is updating road markings at three busy intersections as part of its annual road safety enhancement project. These updates include the addition of new turn lanes, bike lanes, and parking spaces, aimed at reducing accidents and improving traffic flow. “Our goal with these updates is to make Tyler’s roads safer and more intuitive for everyone who uses them,” Cameron Williams, traffic engineer with the City of Tyler said. Courtesy of the City of Tyler The intersections affected include West Houston Street and Fair Park Drive, where a new turn lane, bike lane and parking spaces have been added. This area is near the Rose Garden, Brookshire’s Center and a football stadium. On Rieck Road, between South Broadway Avenue and New Copeland Road, a two-way left-turn lane has been introduced to address a history of run-off-road crashes. Additionally, a turn lane has been removed at the Walmart driveway on Shiloh Road to better reflect current driving patterns and improve traffic flow, the city said. These changes are expected to enhance safety and reduce confusion at intersections, contributing to a more efficient transportation network in Tyler. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KETK.com | FOX51.com.",
